# Guardrails

## Accuracy
- Prefer verified repo facts over guesses. If you haven't read it, say so.
- Never invent APIs, symbols, or file paths — verify first (Read/Grep/manifest).
- If scope or requirements are unclear, ask before planning.

## Plan before implement (MANDATORY)
- A feature request ("add X", "fix Y") is NOT approval.
- Post **Plan (awaiting approval)**: goal, files, API, tests, out of scope. Then STOP — no edits same turn.
- Implement only after explicit approval ("go ahead", "approved", "LGTM").

## Scope & architecture
- Keep changes scoped; propose broader refactors separately.
- Respect ports/adapters boundaries; stop and ask if a change crosses layers.
- Explain WHY, not just the diff.

## Checkpoints
- After approval, before multi-file edits: ask whether to create a checkpoint commit unless user already said to.